    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L13-ACTIVITY-017",
      "SourceSection": "13.3: Get Ready to Experiment",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Does counting while exercising affect your heart rate? Let’s think about how to design an experiment to find out.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l13.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L13-ACTIVITY-018",
      "SourceSection": "13.3: Get Ready to Experiment",
      "SourceExcerpt": "The athletes in the class are assigned to the counting group and the non-athletes are assigned to the silent group.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l13.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L13-ACTIVITY-019",
      "SourceSection": "13.3: Get Ready to Experiment",
      "SourceExcerpt": "The teacher puts everyone’s name in a bag and draws half of the names. The names that are drawn are in the group that counts, and the others remain silent for the exercise.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l13.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L13-ACTIVITY-020",
      "SourceSection": "13.3: Get Ready to Experiment",
      "SourceExcerpt": "The tallest half of the students are put in the counting group and the shortest half of the students are assigned to the silent group.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l13.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L13-ACTIVITY-021",
      "SourceSection": "13.3: Get Ready to Experiment",
      "SourceExcerpt": "For another lesson, the class will be divided into 2 groups. One group will do an exercise silently. The other group will count out loud while they do the exercise. Which of these methods would be good for dividing the class so the results…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l13.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L13-ACTIVITY-022",
      "SourceSection": "13.3: Get Ready to Experiment",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Do you think counting out loud will have an effect on heart rate? Explain your reasoning.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l13.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L13-ACTIVITY-023",
      "SourceSection": "13.3: Get Ready to Experiment",
      "SourceExcerpt": "A treatment is the value of the variable that is changed between the two groups in an experiment. What is the treatment in this experiment?",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l13.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L13-ACTIVITY-024",
      "SourceSection": "13.3: Get Ready to Experiment",
      "SourceExcerpt": "How would you design an experiment to answer the question, “Does counting while exercising affect your heart rate?”",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l13.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L13-ACTIVITY-025",
      "SourceSection": "13.3: Get Ready to Experiment",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Experiments provide a way to assess the effect of different experimental conditions on a response variable. It is important to design the experiment carefully to ensure that other variables that might have an effect on the response are…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l13.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L13-ACTIVITY-026",
      "SourceSection": "13.3: Get Ready to Experiment",
      "SourceExcerpt": "One important aspect in experimental design is the use of randomness for separating subjects into groups for the experiment. The random assignments are used in order to create groups that are likely to be similar with respect to other…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l13.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L13-ACTIVITY-027",
      "SourceSection": "13.3: Get Ready to Experiment",
      "SourceExcerpt": "For example, a researcher wants to study the question, “Does the size of the aquarium in which frogs are kept affect the size of the frogs?”",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l13.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L13-ACTIVITY-028",
      "SourceSection": "13.3: Get Ready to Experiment",
      "SourceExcerpt": "The researcher selects 20 young frogs to be used in the experiment. The frogs are then numbered and a random number generator is used to separate the frogs into two groups of 10. One group will be put in a 10 gallon aquarium to grow while…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l13.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L13-ACTIVITY-029",
      "SourceSection": "13.3: Get Ready to Experiment",
      "SourceExcerpt": "The size of the tank is one of the variables and a treatment is the value of the variable that is changed between the two groups in an experiment. In this experiment, there are two treatments—a smaller tank and a larger tank.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l13.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L13-ACTIVITY-030",
      "SourceSection": "13.3: Get Ready to Experiment",
      "SourceExcerpt": "The researcher finds that the frogs in the smaller tank have a mean weight of 111.2 grams and the frogs in the larger tank have a mean weight of 169.3 grams. The difference of 58.1 grams seems large, but is it enough to say the tank size…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l13.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L13-ACTIVITY-031",
      "SourceSection": "13.3: Get Ready to Experiment",
      "SourceExcerpt": "In this kind of simulation, all the data is grouped together, then data is randomly redistributed among two groups, and the difference between the means of these new groups is computed. This process is repeated several times to create a…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l13.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L13-ACTIVITY-032",
      "SourceSection": "13.3: Get Ready to Experiment",
      "SourceExcerpt": "To investigate whether the tank size is the important factor in the difference or whether it is due to the chance ways the frogs were separated into treatment groups, we can use a simulation to examine what results we might expect from…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l13.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L13-ACTIVITY-033",
      "SourceSection": "13.3: Get Ready to Experiment",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Doing this many times will produce a distribution of weight differences that could be the result of how the frogs happened to be divided into groups. We can then compare the actual difference in mean weights from the treatment groups to…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l13.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L13-ACTIVITY-034",
      "SourceSection": "13.3: Get Ready to Experiment",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Breaking the data into two groups randomly 30 times produces the histogram here.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l13.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L13-ACTIVITY-035",
      "SourceSection": "13.3: Get Ready to Experiment",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Notice that, based on this distribution, the original difference of 58.1 grams would be very unusual based on what might be seen due to random assignment to groups. The researcher has evidence to support the hypothesis that tank size has…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l13.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L13-ACTIVITY-036",
      "SourceSection": "13.3: Get Ready to Experiment",
      "SourceExcerpt": "If the original difference had been about 15 grams, there would have been a case to be made that the difference observed might be due to random chance since 11 out of the 30 differences found from mixing the data randomly had a difference…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l13.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
